# Auth & RBAC

Better Auth is configured in `packages/auth/src/auth.ts`, which exports the `createAuth(cookiePlugin?)` factory (from `@repo/auth/auth`) with the `organization` plugin and `dynamicAccessControl` enabled. A second, optional argument, `runInBackground`, becomes `advanced.backgroundTasks.handler`. The web app builds its instance in `apps/web/src/lib/auth/auth.ts` with `createAuth(nextCookies(), (task) => after(task))` (`after` of `next/server`), so a link's delivery runs after the response and a password reset does not answer later for an account that exists. The tRPC package's instance has no handler: it cannot import Next.js, and the invitations it sends are not a public route. `packages/api/src/auth.ts` builds the tRPC package's instance with `createAuth(nextCookies())` too, not the cookie-less default: the routers call endpoints that set cookies (`changePassword` with `revokeOtherSessions`, `updateUser`, ...), and the plugin forwards those cookies to the browser. Its session reads also extend the session. The browser client is `packages/auth/src/auth-client.ts` (`@repo/auth/auth-client`). Sessions persist in PostgreSQL via Drizzle — tables live in `packages/db/src/schema.ts` (`user`, `session`, `account`, `organization`, `member`, `invitation`, `organizationRole`).

## Reset and invitation links
The blueprint has no mailer. `sendResetPassword` and the organization plugin's `sendInvitationEmail` (both in `packages/auth/src/auth.ts`) hand the link to `deliverLink` in `packages/auth/src/link-delivery.ts`, which logs it to the server console (`[reset-password] <email> → <url>`, `[invitation] <email> → <url>`), in development and in production. In production it also logs `No mailer is configured`: the link is only in the server logs, so a user who forgot a password cannot reset it from their inbox. An invitation link is also shown in the invite dialog, ready to copy. Plug a mail provider (Resend, SES, Postmark, ...) into `deliverLink`, the one place every link leaves the server, before going live.

